<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "https://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    OWASP ZAP (DAST) security suite.

    Isolates OwaspTop10ZapScanTest so a security scan can run on its own weekly
    schedule without dragging in the BDD browser scenarios or the API suites.

    EASIEST PATH - the helper script starts the ZAP daemon, runs this suite, and opens
    the report:

        ./scripts/run-zap-scan.ps1 -Environment staging
        ./scripts/run-zap-scan.ps1 -Environment production

    RUNNING THIS SUITE DIRECTLY - the ZAP daemon must already be up. It sits behind a
    compose profile named "security", so it does NOT start with a plain compose up; see
    the "zap" service in docker-compose.yml for the exact command. Then:

        ./mvnw test "-Dsurefire.suite=testng-security.xml" "-Denv=staging"
        ./mvnw test "-Dsurefire.suite=testng-security.xml" "-Denv=production"

    Staging defaults to a full ACTIVE scan (attack payloads; staging is disposable).
    Production defaults to a baseline PASSIVE scan (read-only; safe against the live
    store). The suite refuses to actively scan production - see OwaspTop10ZapScanTest
    and docs/security-zap.md.

    If ZAP is not running the suite SKIPS rather than fails: the daemon is opt-in
    infrastructure, so a developer running everything locally does not get a red build
    for a service they never asked for.

    parallel="none" is deliberate. The scan itself is a single expensive @BeforeClass;
    the ten category tests are cheap assertions over its in-memory results, so there is
    nothing to gain from threads and a shared ZAP session to corrupt by trying.
-->
<suite name="Timepieces OWASP Top 10 Security Suite" parallel="none">

    <listeners>
        <listener class-name="com.timepieces.automation.listeners.MetricsListener" />
    </listeners>

    <!-- Read by BaseRunner; harmless for a pure TestNG class. OwaspTop10ZapScanTest
         resolves its real target from the env system property via ConfigReader, not
         from this suite parameter. -->
    <parameter name="environment" value="staging" />

    <test name="OWASP Top 10 - ZAP DAST">
        <classes>
            <class name="com.timepieces.automation.tdd.security.OwaspTop10ZapScanTest" />
        </classes>
    </test>
</suite>
